rawosd(1)

# NAME

rawosd - transient feedback renderer for rawm

# SYNOPSIS

*rawosd* [*-C*] [*-c* _path_] [*-v*]

# DESCRIPTION

*rawosd* renders short-lived semantic feedback published by rawm through the
public rawm control membrane. It owns presentation only. Window-manager truth
remains in rawm's *\_RAWM\_STATE* and *\_RAWM\_CLIENTS* snapshots.

The daemon discovers the rawm control selection for the current X screen,
validates protocol version 1, baselines the current *\_RAWM\_FEEDBACK* serial, and
waits for later feedback property changes. It rereads *\_RAWM\_STATE* before
formatting every accepted event.

Starting *rawosd* enables transient presentation; stopping it disables the
presentation. No rawm restart or configuration change is required.

# OPTIONS

*-c* _path_
	Load only the specified configuration file. The path must exist.

*-C*
	Validate the effective configuration and exit without opening the X display.

*-h*
	Print usage and exit.

*-v*
	Print the rawosd version and exit.

# CONFIGURATION

Without *-c*, rawosd layers:

. */etc/rawosd/rawosd.conf*
. *$XDG\_CONFIG\_HOME/rawosd/rawosd.conf*, when *XDG\_CONFIG\_HOME* is an absolute path
. otherwise *~/.config/rawosd/rawosd.conf*

Missing default files are allowed. See *rawosd.conf*(5).

# SIGNALS

*SIGHUP*
	Reload configuration. If parsing, validation, font loading, or color
	allocation fails, rawosd keeps the previous valid configuration.

*SIGINT*, *SIGTERM*
	Exit cleanly.

# RAWM LIFECYCLE

rawosd may start before rawm. While no *\_RAWM\_CONTROL\_SN* owner exists, it waits
without presenting anything. When a compatible owner appears, the current
feedback record is baselined and not replayed.

If the owner disappears, rawosd immediately hides its surface, discards the old
owner XID and feedback serial, and waits for the replacement authority.

# PRESENTATION

The feedback surface is an override-redirect X11 notification window. Placement
uses the work-area geometry published in *\_RAWM\_STATE* version 2. rawosd does
not derive work areas from docks, struts, EWMH properties, or the X window tree.

A newly presented notification is mapped raised. rawosd does not continuously
re-raise it over root-level surfaces that appear later; ordering between
independent override-redirect presentation surfaces remains external to rawosd.
rawm is expected to preserve external transient surfaces when managed clients
are raised.

Live move and resize records are ignored unless *geometry* is enabled in the
rawosd configuration.

# ENVIRONMENT

*DISPLAY*
	X display to use.

*XDG\_CONFIG\_HOME*
	Absolute base path for per-user configuration.

*HOME*
	Fallback base for *~/.config/rawosd/rawosd.conf*.

# FILES

*/etc/rawosd/rawosd.conf*
	System presentation policy.

# SEE ALSO

*rawosd.conf*(5), *rawm*(1)
